# Admin confirmation dialogs

When adding or changing admin features that approve, decline, delete, withdraw, send, or otherwise take an irreversible action:

1. **Do not use** `window.confirm`, `window.alert`, or browser prompts.
2. **Use** `useConfirmDialog` / `ConfirmDialog` from `src/components/admin/ConfirmDialog.jsx`.

```jsx
import { useConfirmDialog } from "../../components/admin/ConfirmDialog";

const { confirm, dialog } = useConfirmDialog();

const ok = await confirm({
  title: "Approve this membership?",
  description: "A confirmation email will be sent to the applicant.",
  confirmLabel: "Approve",
  variant: "success", // success | danger | warning | default
});
if (!ok) return;

// …perform action

return (
  <>
    {/* page UI */}
    {dialog}
  </>
);
```

## Variant guide

- `success` — approve, activate, publish
- `danger` — reject, delete, decline
- `warning` — withdraw, resend, overwrite
- `default` — neutral confirmations

## Copy

- Title: short action question (“Approve this request?”).
- Description: what happens next (email sent, cannot undo, etc.).
- Confirm label: verb matching the action (“Approve”, “Reject”, “Delete”).
